4. Attribution For Mods Built Using YMB

If you publish, distribute, or otherwise make available a mod that was built
using YMB during development, you must provide clear and reasonably visible
attribution to YMB together with a working source link to YMB.

The attribution must appear in a place normally seen by users, downloaders, or
reviewers of that mod, such as a workshop page, repository page, release page,
installer page, project page, README, credits section, or similar public-facing
location.

No exact wording is required. Any truthful attribution that visibly identifies
YMB and includes a working source link is sufficient.

This attribution requirement applies only to public or shared releases of the
built mod and does not apply to purely private or internal use.

